  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 200 AM CDT Fri Aug 7 2026\n\nMid-level high pressure will continue to dominate the period leading \nto warm and mostly rain free conditions outside of isolated \nseabreeze showers. Saturday looks to have the best chance of \nprecipitation as mid-level vorticity riding the periphery of the \nridge will make its way into South Texas at the same time that PWAT \nvalues approach 2.1\" along the immediate coastline. However, QPF \nvalues from any sea breeze storm has lower confidence given the \nvariation of the max PWATs. With the increased cloud cover over the \nweekend, heat index values will struggle to surpass the heat \nadvisory threshold. However, areas that don't experience a sea \nbreeze shower or significant cloud cover may experience heat index \nvalues over 110F. From the start of the workweek, near heat advisory \nconditions return with increasing confidence in the spatial coverage \nof 110F+ values and duration of the peak heat index values.",
